+config OMARCHY_FB_MARKERS
+	bool "omarchy-m5: framebuffer checkpoint markers"
+	depends on ARCH_APPLE
+	help
+	  Paint coloured bands into the framebuffer handed over by the
+	  bootloader at fixed early-boot checkpoints (kernel entry, MMU on,
+	  paging_init, console_init).
+
+	  On a SoC with no working console and no debug cable this is the
+	  only way to distinguish "died in head.S" from "booted fine but has
+	  no console" - both of which look like a frozen bootloader logo.
+
+	  The address below is machine-specific. Bring-up diagnostic only.
+
+config OMARCHY_FB_MARKER_BASE
+	hex "Framebuffer physical base address"
+	depends on OMARCHY_FB_MARKERS
+	default 0x10bd3110000
+	help
+	  Physical address of the framebuffer, as reported by the bootloader
+	  (m1n1 prints it as "fb init: WxH (D) [s=S] @ADDR").
+
+config OMARCHY_FB_MARKER_STRIDE
+	hex "Framebuffer stride in bytes"
+	depends on OMARCHY_FB_MARKERS
+	default 0x2f40
+
+config OMARCHY_FB_MARKER_HEIGHT
+	int "Framebuffer height in pixels"
+	depends on OMARCHY_FB_MARKERS
+	default 1964
+	help
+	  Full panel height (m1n1's "fb init: WxH" before notch hiding). Sizes
+	  the region `earlycon=efifb` draws into, below the marker bands.
